<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldSailScatterer_Register.xml    UtinniPatches · SCALD_MECHANICS_1 S5
  ============================================================================
  Registers RUT_GenStep_ScaldSailScatterer (Defs/MapGeneration/
  RUT_ScaldSailScatterer.xml) onto Base_Player's genSteps — a GenStepDef on
  its own runs on no map, the same fact RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml
  and RUT_Miasma_CrecheScatterer_Register.xml (both this same mod) already
  document and act on. Same three-file shape as both.

  MayRequire on the <li> itself, mirroring RUT_Miasma_CrecheScatterer_
  Register.xml's own precedent — the target GenStepDef only exists when
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is active.

  Global registration is safe for the same reason RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_
  Register.xml's own header gives for its own global registration: the sail
  scatterer's own validator (RM_ScattererValidator_NearThingDef, keyed to
  RUT_ScaldVent) rejects every cell on every map carrying no RUT_ScaldVent
  Things — every biome but the Scald, today.

  Target read from Core directly (Core/Defs/MapGeneration/
  BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml:4-15, MapGeneratorDef ParentName="MapCommonBase"
  Name="Base_Player", <genSteps> a plain <li> list) — same citation this
  mod's own prior registrations already give. Conditional test xpath is
  identical to the inner Add's xpath (this mod's own established discipline
  for a silent no-op instead of a red error if Core ever restructures the
  node).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">RUT_GenStep_ScaldSailScatterer</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
